window.WIKI_ENTRY={"id": "concept-087", "name_zh": "自发性", "name_en": "spontaneity", "tagline": "赛斯的内在宇宙第三条基本法则：一切意识都自发地存在于广阔的现在；自发性知道它自己的秩序，真正的纪律恰是自发的结果", "explanation": "在赛斯的体系里，自发性（spontaneity）首先是宇宙论的，其次才是心理学的。他把它列为内在宇宙的第三条基本法则：一切意识都自发地存在于「广阔的现在」之中，你看到的因果先后，只是你把自发的行动用慢镜头接收出来的幻觉。因此「秩序」不是管出来的——「自发性知道它自己的秩序」，身体自发地长出并修复自己全部部件，是这条法则最现成的证据。落到个人层面，赛斯反复指出人们恰恰从小被教导去害怕自己的自发（家庭、教堂、学校合谋），把它当成失控与危险；而他给出的方向是反的：你的安全就在自发性里，自发性的自己会自我修正，真正的纪律是自发的结果，而不是它的对立面。这一页与「冲动」相邻但不同：冲动讲那股驱策力本身，自发性讲的是不被预设框住、让能量按自己的节奏成形的行动品质。", "definitions": [{"zh": "这里，你可能看出我们正要讨论什么了。我们的内在宇宙第三条基本法则是自发性（spontaneity），不管开始和结束的所有表象，也不管死亡与衰败的所有表象，所有的意识都以自发的方式存在于广阔的现在之内，存在于同时的和谐之中，然而，在广阔的现在之内也有面耐久性。", "en": "You may see what we are getting into here. Our third law is spontaneity, and despite all appearances of beginning and end, despite all appearances of death and decay, all consciousness exists in the spacious present, in a spontaneous manner, in simultaneous harmony, and yet within the spacious present there is also durability.", "source": "Session 44"}, {"zh": "不过，许多人害怕自发性：它唤起放肆、过分，及危险的自由。即使不那么热烈地反对自发性的人，也往往觉得它不知怎地可疑、讨厌，也许导向令人蒙羞的行为。可是，自发性代表生命本身的精神，而它是活下去的意志，和激发行为、动作及发现的那些冲动的基础。", "en": "Many people, however, fear spontaneity: it evokes extravagance, excesses, and dangerous freedoms. Even people who are not so fervently opposed to spontaneity often feel that it is somehow suspect, distasteful, perhaps leading to humiliating actions. Spontaneity, however, represents the spirit of life itself, and it is the basis for the will to live, and for those impulses that stimulate action, motion, and discovery.", "source": "Session 10"}, {"zh": "所以，相信自发性与纪律只是相反的东西是错误的。反之，真正的纪律是真正自发的结果。", "en": "It is erroneous, therefore, to believe that spontaneity and discipline are mere opposites. Instead, true discipline is the result of true spontaneity.", "source": "Session 10"}], "blocks": [{"id": "B01", "title": "赛斯列的「第三条基本法则」就是自发性", "note": "赛斯在早期课第 44 节给内在宇宙立法，第三条法则直接写成自发性：不管表面上有没有开始、结束、死亡、衰败，所有意识都以自发的方式存在于广阔的现在。他又把自发性列为那个「价值气候」的主要属性之一，说它只在唯一真正有意义的时间——广阔的现在——里展现。另一处他还点名：一旦广阔的现在带着它的自发性被了解，因果论就落幕。所以在这里自发性不是「随性而为」的心情，而是赛斯对存在本身运作方式的正式表述。", "src": "第 44、41、45、51、744 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 44 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 41 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 45 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 51 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 744 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-087-e0011", "zh": "这里，你可能看出我们正要讨论什么了。我们的内在宇宙第三条基本法则是自发性（spontaneity），不管开始和结束的所有表象，也不管死亡与衰败的所有表象，所有的意识都以自发的方式存在于广阔的现在之内，存在于同时的和谐之中，然而，在广阔的现在之内也有面耐久性。", "en": "You may see what we are getting into here. Our third law is spontaneity, and despite all appearances of beginning and end, despite all appearances of death and decay, all consciousness exists in the spacious present, in a spontaneous manner, in simultaneous harmony, and yet within the spacious present there is also durability.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第44节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "44", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0009", "zh": "这个值气候的主要属性之一是自发性，它在唯一具有任何真实意义的那种时间的存在之中展现，也就是广阔的现在。", "en": "One of the main attributes of this value climate is spontaneity, that shows itself in the existence of the only sort of time that has any real meaning, that of the spacious present.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第44节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "44", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0007", "zh": "在广阔的现在之中，正如它确实存在的样子，所有已经存在的东西仍然存在，所有在你们的未来将会存在的也已然确实存在了。在你们的层面，除非透过一种非常限制的方式，否则你们不能经验这样的实相，而且你们也无法自发地经验这种实相，自发性是广阔的现在的一项特性。以你们伪装时间的观念来看，你们或许会觉得，这些资料听起来很奇怪，令人难以置信。", "en": "In the spacious present as it exists in actuality beyond shadow, all things that have existed still exist, and all things that shall exist in your tomorrow already do exist. You on your plane cannot experience such reality except in a very limited manner, and you cannot experience such reality spontaneously, and spontaneity is the quality of the spacious present. To you with your ideas of camouflage time this material may sound strange and unbelievable.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第41节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "41", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0010", "zh": "广阔的现在与耐久性（durability）的存在并不矛盾，而耐久性没有暗含你们以为的一个未来的存在。现在，这看起来可能矛盾，但稍后，我希望你们能更清楚地了解这一点。广阔的现在，虽然自发性地存在、虽然同时发生，但在它之内仍包含耐久的（duration）性质。", "en": "The spacious present does not contradict the existence of durability, but durability does not imply the existence of a future as you conceive it. Now this may appear contradictory, but later I hope that you will understand this more clearly. The spacious present, while existing spontaneously, while happening simultaneously, still contains within it qualities of duration.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第44节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "44", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0014", "zh": "回来稍微说一下，我想再提提我们广阔的现在，一切万物在其中都有它们的存在。一旦这广阔的现在，带着它的自发性（spontaneity）被了解了，因果论就会落幕。持续性（continuity）造成的因果论，是站不住脚的。基本上，你们知道，广阔的现在的确有耐久性（durability），因为有价值完成的存在。", "en": "Now returning briefly, I would like again to mention our spacious present, in which all things have their existence. When the spacious present is understood, with its attributes of spontaneity, then the cause and effect theory will fall. The cause and effect theory being the result of continuity holds no water. Basically, the spacious present as you know does have durability, because of the existence of value fulfillment.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第51节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "51", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0015", "zh": "就“持续性”这个词的一般用法而言，它是没有持续性的。“持续性”通常隐含一件事发生在另一件之前或之后的意思。广阔的现在反而包含自发性，而且在它之内，所有的发生都是同时的，但又有耐久性。", "en": "It does not have continuity, in the manner in which the term continuity is usually used. Continuity usually implies one thing happening before or after another. The spacious present contains instead spontaneity, and within it all happenings are simultaneous, and yet there is durability.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第51节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "51", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0016", "zh": "然而，关于持久的自发性还有很多要谈论的。我也说过，你自己目前的存在同时发生。你只是以慢动作感知它。", "en": "There is much yet to be covered dealing with a spontaneity that is nevertheless durable. I have also said that your own present existence occurs simultaneously. You only perceive it in slow motion.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第54节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "54", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0210", "zh": "这个价值气候的一个主要属性就是自发性，它只在唯一真正有意义的那种时间——即广阔的现在——即存在里显示它自己。", "en": "One of the main attributes of this value climate is spontaneity, which shows itself in the existence of the only sort of time that has any real meaning — that of the spacious present.", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第744节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "744", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0211", "zh": "在此，你们可以看出我们将谈到的是什么。我们的第三个定律是自发性，而不管所有开始与结束、死亡与腐败之表象，所有的意识都以一种自发的方式，以同时性的和谐存在于一个广阔的现在；然而，在广阔的现在之内也有耐久性。", "en": "You may see what we are getting at here. Our third law is spontaneity, and despite all appearances of beginning and end, of death and decay, all consciousnesses exist in the spacious present, in a spontaneous manner, in simultaneous harmony; and yet within the spacious present there is also durability.", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第744节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "744", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B02", "title": "不是因果链，是自发性的秩序", "note": "赛斯说你们层面看起来讲因果，那本身是一种必要的伪装——事实上没有你以为的因果效应，有的只是自发性。行动基本是自发性的，前后结果发生得太快，说不清谁引发谁；你像用慢镜头看一场爆炸那样接收它，才产生了「连续时间」的错觉。他强调这不是混乱：宇宙是一个群体共享的梦，建立在自发的秩序上而不是混乱上；架构二把秩序与自发性合在一起；「自发性知道它自己的秩序」是他反复回来的那句话。", "src": "第 40、214、700、772、826、898、937 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 40 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 214 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 700 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 772 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 826 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 898 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 937 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-087-e0006", "zh": "你们的层面是能量操纵应用的训练场地。你们的层面似乎在处理因果，但这本身是一种必要的伪装。事实上，并没有你们所认为的因果效应。有的只是自发性而已。每隔一段特定的时间，你们必须学到仿佛有因果现象存在，以便使自发性的结果不会以混乱做结果。这样的说法也许好像有点矛盾，但以后你们会知道其实不会。", "en": "Your plane is a training place in the use of manipulation of energy. Your plane seems to deal with cause and effect, but this is in itself a necessary camouflage. In actuality there is no cause and effect as you think of it. There is only spontaneity. For a particular interval you must be taught as if there were cause and effect, so that the result of spontaneity would not end up as chaos. This statement may seem contradictory but later you will see that it is not.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第40节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "40", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0008", "zh": "没有一个连续的片刻点，也可以有秩序。没有你们的因果关系，信不信由你，也一样可以有秩序。在自发性里、在广阔的现在的同时性存在里，也可以有秩序，而且的确也有了秩序。", "en": "There can be order without a succession of moments. There can be order, believe it or not, without your cause and effect. There can be order, and there is order, in spontaneity, and in the simultaneous existence of the spacious present.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第41节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "41", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0076", "zh": "如同我告诉过你们的，所有的行动基本上都是自发性的。只有你对它的感知给行动添加了时间的幻觉。比如说，你认为任何特定的行动都会消耗、吞噬或占用一定量的时间。因此你认为时间是某种包含行动的东西。", "en": "As I have told you, all action is basically spontaneous. Only your perception of it adds the illusion of time to action. You think, for example, that any given action consumes or devours or takes up a certain amount of time. Therefore you think of time as something that contains action.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第214节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "214", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0077", "zh": "再次地，行动基本上是自发性的，而结果发生的如此迅速，以至于不可能去说哪一个发生在前、哪一个发生在后，或哪一个引发了哪一个。这可以比喻成某些非常迅速发生的、庞大的、自发性的动作。当你以慢镜头检视这个庞大的动作，你会在你们系统里一个连续性的时间内接收到结果。事实上，当一个突然的爆炸发生的时候，你会看到光和动作的一个缓慢进程。", "en": "For the actions are spontaneous basically, again, and the effects exist so swiftly that it is impossible to say that one occurs before or after the other, or causes another. This could be likened to some gigantic, spontaneous motion that happens very swiftly. When you viewed such a gigantic motion with a slow camera, then you would get the effect that you receive within your system, of a continuous time. Where actually perhaps a sudden explosion had taken place, you would see a slow progression of light and motion.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第214节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "214", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0197", "zh": "只当作一个比喻，让我们这么来看：你们现在的宇宙是一个为群体共享的梦，颇具有效性——以某种角度来表现实相的一个梦；这个梦最重要的是，它是有意义的、具创造性的，而且，并非建立在混乱上（以一个会心的眼色），却是建立在自发性的秩序上。可是，若要了解它，你必须去到意识的另一个层面——在那儿，也许，梦暂时的看来仿佛不那么的真实似的。从另外一个角度，在那儿，你甚至可以更清楚的看它，把它当作你手中的一张照片一样，同时，你也可由那更广的视角看到，你也的确是站在梦的范畴之外，但却又是在另一个“里面”里，而因为照片本身的限制，那是无法在照片里显出来的。", "en": "Simply as an analogy, look at it this way: Your present universe is a mass-shared dream, quite valid — a dream that presents reality in a certain light; a dream that is above all meaningful, creative, based not upon chaos (with a knowing look), but upon spontaneous order. To understand it, however, you must go to another level of consciousness — one where, perhaps, the dream momentarily does not seem so real. There, from another viewpoint, you can see it even more clearly, holding it like a photograph in your hands; at the same time you can see from that broader perspective that you do indeed also stand outside of the dream context, but in a “within” that cannot show in the snapshot because of its limitations.", "source": "未知的实相卷一 · 第700节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷一", "session": "700", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0239", "zh": "当然，十分可能，你可预知的世界，并不因为那些令人惊奇的、不可预知的、非官方的事件而无法存在，反之却正因它们而得以存在。有一种更大的自发性秩序，而你们世界那仿佛不可预知的成分，为这秩序提供了它们自己的线索。", "en": "It is instead, of course, quite possible that your predictable world exists not in spite of but because of those surprising, unpredictable, unofficial occurrences. Period. There is a kind of larger spontaneous order of which the seemingly unpredictable elements of your world provide their own clues.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第937节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "937", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0231", "zh": "不过，当你检查梦境时，通常你都是从醒时实相的架构去那样做。你试图应用你通常判断事件标准的实相规则，去度量梦经验的幅度，所以，你没办法感知梦境的真实特性。除了在那些稀有的场合，当你在你的梦境之中“变得觉醒”时——我们在本书稍后会讨论这件事。但以一种说法，说宇宙是以你自己的思想与梦境发生的同样的方式被创造出来是真的：自发性的，却又有一个天生固有的令人惊异的秩序，以及一个内在的组织。你想你的思想，作你的梦，而对其中涉及的不可置信的过程没有任何清晰的知识。然而，那些过程正是在宇宙的存在本身背后的过程。", "en": "When you examine the state of dreams, however, you do it as a rule from the framework of waking reality. You try to measure the dimension of dream experience by applying the rules of reality that are your usual criteria for judging events. Therefore, you are not able to perceive the true characteristics of the dreaming state except on those few occasions when you “come awake” within your dreams—a matter we will discuss later on in this book. But in a manner of speaking, it is true to say that the universe was created in the same fashion that your own thoughts and dreams happen: spontaneously and yet with a built-in amazing order, and an inner organization. You think your thoughts and you dream your dreams without any clear knowledge of the incredible processes involved therein, yet those processes are the very ones that are behind the existence of the universe itself.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第898节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "898", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0232", "zh": "同时，以一种说法，你自己就是那将你们的世界梦入存在的古老做梦者。你必须了解，我并没有说你们是被动的、倏忽即逝的梦者，失落在某个神圣的心智里；而是说你是一个神圣智慧之独特的创造性示现，那个神圣智慧之创造力为所有的实相负责，而那些实相本身被赋予它们自己的创造能力，且带着想要圆满的潜力及愿望——那神圣过程本身的继承者。自发性知道它自己的秩序。", "en": "Also, in a manner of speaking, you are yourselves the ancient dreamers who dreamed your world into being. You must understand that I am not saying that you are passive, fleeting dreamers, lost in some divine mind, but that you are the unique creative manifestations of a divine intelligence whose creativity is responsible for all realities, which are themselves endowed with creative abilities of their own, with the potential and desire for fulfillment—inheritors indeed of the divine processes themselves. Spontaneity knows its own order.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第898节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "898", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0214", "zh": "一般而言，理性与理智于是被认作是男性特质（Generally, reason and intellect are then considered male qualities），以及是文明、科学和组织化的世界之构架。直觉与冲动则被认作是反复无常的、不可靠的、女性的，而该被控制。世界因为自发性而存在。文明因为人们想要在一起的冲动而开始，它自发的生长而进入秩序。你只看到许多过程的外表，因为你们客观化的观点不允许你认同更多内容的显示。在你看来，似乎所有的系统在某个时候都崩溃——变得较无秩序或流入混乱之中。", "en": "Generally, reason and intellect are then considered male qualities, and the frameworks for civilization, science, and an organized world. The intuitions and the impulses are considered erratic, untrustworthy, feminine, and to be controlled. The world exists because of spontaneous order. Civilization began because of the impulse of people to be together. It grew spontaneously and came into order. You only see the outside of many processes because your objectified viewpoint does not allow you the identification that would show you more. It seems to you then that all systems sometime break down — become less orderly or fall into chaos.", "source": "心灵的本质 · 第772节", "year": "1975–77", "tag": null, "short": "心灵的本质", "session": "772", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0219", "zh": "若非如此，你们自己的种族不会存在得像它已经存在的这么久。而文明的构成——艺术、商业、甚或科技——也不会可能。“架构二”结合了秩序与自发性，但它的秩序是属于另外一种的。那秩序是一种圆形的、联想性的、“自然有秩序”的过程，在其中，自发性自动存在于最能完成意识的潜能之整体秩序内。", "en": "If that were not the case, your own species would not have existed as long as it has. Nor would the constructs of civilization — art, commerce, or even technology — have been possible. Framework 2 combines order and spontaneity, but its order is of another kind. It is a circular, associative, “naturally ordering process,” in which spontaneity automatically exists in the overall order that will best fulfill the potentials of consciousness.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第826节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "826", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0208", "zh": "某些家族特别喜欢在某些月分里出生，但并没有明确的规则可以适用。的确有一种内在的秩序统一所有这些问题：但那内在的秩序并非定律的结果，却是自发性的创造之结果，流入成它自己的那种模式。你看到在任何既定时候的模式，而试着由它们造出定律。", "en": "Certain families have a liking for certain months of birth,4 but no specific rules apply. There is indeed an inner kind of order that unites all of these issues; yet that inner order is not the result of laws, but of spontaneous creation, which flows into its own kinds of patterns. You see the patterns at any given time and try to make laws of them.", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第740节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "740", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0203", "zh": "物质上而言，一株植物的种子落到地上，它们也许被吹到离出生地有段距离的地方，但心灵的“种子”却也飞进其它的实相。不过，在所有这些之内，在自发性与秩序之间有一个最精致的平衡。紫罗兰不会在冬天生长，只有当某些条件合适时，它们的特性才会出现。所以，如果你是在一九四〇年生的，你在跟随你自己的时间上没有问题，而你在那些你出生时的一般条件下成就你自己的人生。", "en": "Physically, the seeds of a plant fall onto the earth. They may be blown to some place distant from their birth, but the psyche’s “seeds” fly into other realities also. Within all of this, however, there is the finest balance between spontaneity and order. Violets do not grow in wintertime. Their characteristics appear only when certain conditions are met. So if you were born in 1940 you have no trouble keeping track of your own time, and you fulfill your life under the same general conditions as those in which you were born.", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第728节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "728", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B03", "title": "身体是自发秩序最现成的证据", "note": "在《健康之道》里赛斯把这条宇宙论落到你身上：身体意识的主要特征就是自发性，所以它能以意识心根本处理不了的速度运作；看见这个动作和所有感官都依赖这份内在自发。你的呼吸、思考、修补伤口，全都在你正常有意识的注意之下自发完成。他的结论很硬：没有比自发长出自己全部部件的肉体更高度有系统的东西——你身上那份秩序恰恰不是管出来的，是自发出来的。", "src": "第 1、10、40、631、728、815 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 1 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 10 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 40 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 631 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 728 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 815 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-087-e0244", "zh": "鲁柏怕它会按照它自己的理由去行动，那可能不是鲁柏自己的——或他以为如此。现在他开始了解，他的能量是他生命的礼物——要被表达，而非抑制——并且再次的了解，自发性知道它自己的秩序。", "en": "He was afraid that it acted according to its own reasons which might not be his own — or so he thought. Now he is beginning to understand that his energy is the gift of his life — to be expressed, not repressed — and to understand, again, that spontaneity knows its own order.", "source": "健康之道 · 第1节", "year": "1984", "tag": null, "short": "健康之道", "session": "1", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0263", "zh": "自然及人的内在本质两者都被视为包含着野蛮、破坏性的力量，文明和理性必须坚定地与之抗衡。科学本身往往展示强迫性的和仪式性的行为，竟至编排其自己的推理路径，以便它们含括安全领域，而固定地忽略那使得科学——或任何别的学科——成为可能的自发性伟大内在力量。如我先前说过的，自发性明白它自己的秩序。再没有比自发地生长其自己所有部分的肉体更高度有系统的了。", "en": "Nature and the inner nature of man are both seen to contain savage, destructive forces against which civilization and the reasoning mind must firmly stand guard. Science itself often displays compulsive and ritualistic behavior, to the point of programming its own paths of reasoning, so that they cover safe ground, and steadfastly ignore the great inner forces of spontaneity that make science — or any discipline — possible. As I have said before, spontaneity knows its own order. Nothing is more highly organized than the physical body that spontaneously grows all of its own parts.", "source": "健康之道 · 第10节", "year": "1984", "tag": null, "short": "健康之道", "session": "10", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0246", "zh": "身体意识之主要特征就是其自发性。（停顿良久。）这允许它以一种不可置信的速度运作，那是心智最顶级的有意识部分所无法处理的。它的运作乃由于一种几乎是瞬间的意识，在其间，知道的东西被知道了，而在知者与所知者之间，可说是没有距离的。", "en": "The main characteristic of bodily consciousness is its spontaneity. (Long pause.) This allows it to work at an incredibly swift rate that could not be handled by the topmost conscious portions of the mind. Its operation is due to an almost instantaneous kind of consciousness, in which what is known is known, with no distance between, say, the knower and the known.", "source": "健康之道 · 第1节", "year": "1984", "tag": null, "short": "健康之道", "session": "1", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0247", "zh": "“看见”这动作，以及所有身体的感官，都依赖这内在的自发性。", "en": "The act of seeing, and all of the body’s senses, are dependent upon this inner spontaneity.", "source": "健康之道 · 第1节", "year": "1984", "tag": null, "short": "健康之道", "session": "1", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0256", "zh": "你肉身存在的本身就是依赖许多自发性的过程的平顺运作。你的思想、呼吸及运动，全都被大半是无意识的活动——至少从你平常想作是意识心的观点来看——所指导。", "en": "Your very physical existence itself is dependent upon the smooth functioning of many spontaneous processes. Your thinking, breathing, and motion are all guided by activities that are largely unconscious — at least from the standpoint of what you usually think of as the conscious mind.", "source": "健康之道 · 第10节", "year": "1984", "tag": null, "short": "健康之道", "session": "10", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0257", "zh": "你的身体经常不断地修补它们自己，而你的头脑会思想——全都没在你正常有意识的注意之下。这也适用于所有那些使得生命变得可能的内在过程上。你的思想是有意识的，但思考的过程本身则否。在儿童的行为里，以及在他们肢体自然的节奏性活动里，自发性尤其重要。情感也仿佛以一种自发性的方式来来去去。", "en": "Your body repairs itself constantly, and your mind thinks — all without your normally conscious attention. The same applies to all of those inner processes that make life possible. Your thoughts are conscious, but the process of thinking itself is not. Spontaneity is particularly important in the actions of children, and in the natural rhythmic motion of their limbs. Feelings also seem to come and go in a spontaneous fashion.", "source": "健康之道 · 第10节", "year": "1984", "tag": null, "short": "健康之道", "session": "10", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0258", "zh": "的确没错，好像人格的某些自发性部分，远比我们如此有理由感到骄傲的有意识部分，还要来得有知识。", "en": "It is indeed as if some inner spontaneous part of the personality is far more knowledgeable than the conscious portion of which we are so rightfully proud.", "source": "健康之道 · 第10节", "year": "1984", "tag": null, "short": "健康之道", "session": "10", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0217", "zh": "无疑的，在那方面每一件事都为你的利益在运作。的确，常常当你变得对你的身体愈关切的时候，它的运作就愈不顺利。在你身体运作的自发性里，很显然的，有一种微妙的秩序感。当你打开了一台电视，画面好像不知道从什么地方跑到荧幕上——但那个画面却是精密的集中焦点的秩序之结果。", "en": "In that regard, certainly, everything works to your advantage. Indeed, often the more concerned you become with your body the less smoothly it functions. In the spontaneity of your body’s operation there is obviously a fine sense of order. When you turn on a television set the picture seems to come out of nowhere onto the screen — yet that picture is the result of order precisely focused.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第815节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "815", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0186", "zh": "在身体自发性的机能里，你看见灵魂轻易的流动性，那“随着本然的我而行”的特性，是对灵魂内在自由的指标，却又指明其天生的方向感。身体实相的所有各部分，是灵魂实相在肉体里的版本，就像外在宇宙所有各区段“镜照”一个内在的宇宙，后者就与外在世界一样的活生生、自然和多变。物理现象只是所谓的自然之一部分，而所有实相皆是自然的。", "en": "In the body’s spontaneous functioning you see the easy mobility of the soul, the “going with that which I am,” which is an indication of the soul’s inner freedom and yet innate sense of direction. All portions of the body’s reality are versions in flesh of the soul’s reality, even as all segments of the exterior universe mirror an internal one. The latter is as alive and natural and changing as the exterior world. Physical phenomena is only a portion of what nature is, and all realities are natural.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第631节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "631", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0204", "zh": "口授。最细小植物的根知道生长之最佳条件为何，而自发性的伸向最圆满的发展之可能性。", "en": "(Resume at 10:35.) Dictation: The roots of the tiniest plant know the best conditions for their growth, and they reach spontaneously toward the most fulfilling probabilities for development.", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第728节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "728", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0005", "zh": "如果给了蜘蛛自我和理智，那你们可以想见会是怎样的一个画面。这会让它扩大了觉知和活动的范围，但同时也会造成阻碍，使得它的蜘蛛网，不再是那么直接从它的源头而来，或是那么具有自发性。", "en": "Give the spider an ego and an intellect and you will see then how the picture would change. These would enable him to enlarge upon his scope of awareness and activity, but at the same time impediments would be placed so that the web construction would no longer appear either as direct as far as its source is concerned, nor as spontaneous.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第40节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "40", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B04", "title": "自发性与纪律不是敌人，真正的纪律是自发的结果", "note": "这是赛斯讲得最多的一组张力：他和鲁柏的课要维持「自发与纪律之间一种微妙的平衡」。规律是必要的，但不要死板——只要自动到来的自发，以及在纪律之内达成的自由。他甚至说这是个悖论：恰恰在自发性的基础上，授课的那份规律才立得住。到最后他把话说透：以为自发性与纪律只是相反的东西是错的，真正的纪律是真正自发的结果。对普通读者的意思是：想要生活有章法，办法不是把自己越管越紧。", "src": "第 58、62、78、132、134、394、441、467、506 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 58 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 62 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 78 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 132 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 134 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 394 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 441 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 467 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 506 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-087-e0264", "zh": "就如你的生命是由这些自发过程提供给你的，可以这样说，宇宙的生命也是以同样方式提供的。你看见物质的星辰，而你们的仪器探入遥远的太空——但，使得宇宙成为可能的“内在过程”，是那些推进你自己思维的同样过程。所以，相信自发性与纪律只是相反的东西是错误的。反之，真正的纪律是真正自发的结果。", "en": "(All intently:) As your life is provided for you, so to speak, by these spontaneous processes, the life of the universe is provided in the same fashion. You see the physical stars, and your instruments probe the distances of space — but the inner processes that make the universe possible are those same processes that propel your own thinking. It is erroneous, therefore, to believe that spontaneity and discipline are mere opposites. Instead, true discipline is the result of true spontaneity.", "source": "健康之道 · 第10节", "year": "1984", "tag": null, "short": "健康之道", "session": "10", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0037", "zh": "我们目前在我们的课里有很多的自发和自由。很多，纯粹因为我们是在一个纪律的架构之内工作。", "en": "We now have a good deal of spontaneity and freedom within our sessions. A good deal, simply because we are working within a framework of discipline.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第132节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "132", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0039", "zh": "因为没有反抗的天性，你们两人都不会准许这些课开始出现。所有的创造力都来自这个组合。我们定期上课的规律现在是必要的。但这并不是说不可以偶尔不上课，或是一节不上应该被当成是一个重大的症状。整体而言，我们的时间表将会继续维持，但我们不想要死板，只想要自动到来的自发，以及在纪律之内达成的自由。", "en": "For without a rebellious nature neither of you would have permitted the sessions to begin. From this mixture all creativity comes. Our regularity of sessions is now a necessity. This does not mean however that at times a session cannot be missed, or that such a missed session should be considered a significant symptom. Overall our schedule will be maintained, but we do not want rigidity, merely the spontaneity that comes, and the freedom that is achieved within discipline.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第134节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "134", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0021", "zh": "虽然如此，我不只是想到鲁柏，也想要让你在为资料打字这事上面休息一下，约瑟，而且我关心给你更多时间消化手上资料的事。我不知道你会变得这么在意。我真的感到受宠若惊。自发与纪律之间有一种微妙的平衡，我试着让这些课保持流动、流畅、有纪律，但也要透过自发赋予它们生命。", "en": "Nevertheless I am not only thinking of Ruburt, but also I wanted to give you some rest Joseph, in typing the material, and I was concerned with giving you more time to assimilate material as you get it. I did not realize that you would become so concerned. I am indeed flattered. There is a delicate balance here of spontaneity and discipline, and I try to keep the sessions fluid, fluent, disciplined and yet also to give them life through spontaneity.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第62节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "62", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0018", "zh": "必须保持微妙的平衡，但能量将会来到你身上。你还是必须许下更热情的誓言，投入整个世界之中，认同在它之内以及属于它的万事万物，因为你有时会退缩。但是从这热情的投入誓言，将会榨出最后的高度孤立与理解，从中产生你最好的作品。一定要有带着纪律的一种热情的喜悦与自发。", "en": "There is a delicate balance to be maintained, but energy will come to you. You must still make a more passionate oath of involvement with the world at large, and identification with everything within it, and of it, for you have sometimes shrunk from this. But from this passionate oath of involvement will be wrung the final intense isolation and comprehension from which your best work will come. There must be, with discipline, a passionate joyfulness and spontaneity.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第58节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "58", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0019", "zh": "这种纪律、孤立和决心，与自发、喜悦和投入的组合，我再怎么强调也不为过。在你的情况中，你有必要把你的能力运用到外在世界，这对你有极大的益处。你不知道当你不那么故步自封的时候，你自己的人格对其他人有什么样的影响。", "en": "I cannot stress too deeply this mixture of spontaneity, joyfulness and involvement with discipline, isolation and determination. In your case the involvement, the necessity for using your abilities in the outside world, also are extremely beneficial. You have no idea of the effect of your own personality upon others when you do not hold back.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第58节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "58", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0022", "zh": "这个概念应该是一种抽象的哲学思想。至少这个是可由最初有意识的意图达成的。对一个抽象本质的冥想往往能更进一步导向有效的心灵体验。你们也许可以试试这个当作调节剂。在必要的条件反射、仪式、习惯、自发性、自由和我们将称之为瞬间心灵放松之间，永远要有一个平衡。", "en": "The idea should be an abstract philosophical concept. This at least, can be done by initial conscious intent. Contemplation of an abstract nature often leads further into valid psychic experience. You may try this for a change of pace. There must always be a balance between necessary conditioning, ritual and habit, and spontaneity, freedom, and what we will call instantaneous psychic relaxations.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第78节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "78", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0147", "zh": "鲁柏有时觉得——不太合理地，因为你曾告诉他并非如此——你认为他缺课时是在逃避。课需要规律，也需要自发性，而就他自己的天性而言，我尽量让这两种需要都得到满足。这是为了我们的课着想，也是为了整体的平衡与效率。", "en": "Now Ruburt feels, at times unreasonably, for you have told him differently, that you think he shirks when he misses sessions. The sessions need regularity. They also need spontaneity, and for his own nature, I try to see that both needs are met. This is for the benefit of our sessions and for overall balance and efficiency.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第441节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "441", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0146", "zh": "他明白一个特定的时间更为实际。他很享受昨晚那堂自发的课（为珍星期二晚上的ESP班而开），这样的课虽然对我们的资料没有特别的增添，却能补足他的创作努力，给他一种自由感。自发性常常——虽非总是——有助于凝聚他的能力，并为我们提供极佳的出神状态。自发性自会提供它自己的训练。你也许注意到，常常在你们错过常规课的时候，我会在班上举行一堂自发的课。", "en": "He realizes that a specific time is more practical. He enjoyed last evening's spontaneous session (for Jane's Tuesday night ESP class), and such sessions, while they do not particularly add to our material, replenish his creative efforts and give him a sense of freedom. The spontaneity often, though not always, helps to focus his abilities, and provides us with an excellent trance state. The spontaneity provides its own training. You may have noticed that often when you miss a regular session, I have held a spontaneous one in class.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第441节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "441", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0154", "zh": "我们课的规律性很重要。一定的自由与自发性也同样重要。", "en": "The regularity of our sessions is important. Some freedom and spontaneity is also important.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第467节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "467", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0167", "zh": "好。（停顿——今晚这样的停顿有许多次。）鲁柏[Ruburt]不必为了错过几次定时的课而担忧。他一直在运用自发性；而说来矛盾，我们授课的那份规律，恰恰就有赖于这份自发性。你们明白我的意思吗？", "en": "Now. (Pause, one of many.) Ruburt need not worry that he has missed a few regular sessions. He has been exercising spontaneity, and paradoxically enough it is upon spontaneity that the regularity of our sessions depends. Do you follow me?", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第506节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "506", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0113", "zh": "可以举行自发性的课程，但整个定期课也应该继续下去。沟通管道已经打开，一般而言，更深入、更彻底的接触将随着这些相同的方式而来。对鲁柏来讲，在这种惯常的定期课当中，甚至会有一定的安全感和舒适感，这会使他能举行一些精彩绝伦的课程。", "en": "Spontaneous sessions may be held, but the overall routine should be continued. The channels have been opened, and as a rule, deeper and stronger contact will follow these same patterns. There is even for Ruburt a certain security and comfort in this accustomed routine, that will allow him to hold some truly spectacular sessions.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第394节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "394", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B05", "title": "你为什么会怕自己的自发：学校、教堂与家庭怎么教的", "note": "赛斯说很多人怕自发性，因为它唤起放肆、过分与「危险的自由」的感觉——而这份恐惧是被教出来的。自我害怕自发，因为它控制不了行动；有组织宗教与教条把自发与失控画上等号；鲁柏从小被周围人警告自己的热情「可怕」，母亲说他情绪高涨时会发疯，从此任何自发都让他联想到危险。连科学与理性文明也配合演出：凡是「自发」发生的事都被投以怀疑的眼光。赛斯的定性很反直觉：人跟自己天性作对，恰恰是在自己心智里被布置好的。", "src": "第 146、320、421、588、714、845 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 146 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 320 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 421 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 588 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 714 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 845 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-087-e0259", "zh": "不过，许多人害怕自发性：它唤起放肆、过分，及危险的自由。即使不那么热烈地反对自发性的人，也往往觉得它不知怎地可疑、讨厌，也许导向令人蒙羞的行为。可是，自发性代表生命本身的精神，而它是活下去的意志，和激发行为、动作及发现的那些冲动的基础。", "en": "Many people, however, fear spontaneity: it evokes extravagance, excesses, and dangerous freedoms. Even people who are not so fervently opposed to spontaneity often feel that it is somehow suspect, distasteful, perhaps leading to humiliating actions. Spontaneity, however, represents the spirit of life itself, and it is the basis for the will to live, and for those impulses that stimulate action, motion, and discovery.", "source": "健康之道 · 第10节", "year": "1984", "tag": null, "short": "健康之道", "session": "10", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0043", "zh": "自我也害怕自发，因为它无法控制行动；身为行动的一部分，它的努力大部分必然受挫。但就是介于自我奋力求取稳定，以及人格想要自发扩展的企图之间的这种挣扎，是人类大部分成就的基础，当然也是他大部分艺术的根据。", "en": "Ego also fears spontaneity, for it cannot control action; being a part of action, most of its efforts of necessity are thwarted. Yet it is precisely this struggle between ego’s struggles for stability, and the personality’s attempt to expand spontaneously, that is at the basis of much of mankind’s achievements, and that is certainly the basis for much of his art.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第146节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "146", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0261", "zh": "只不过因为文明人多少过分强调运用一种知识来超越另一种，使得人们害怕自己无意识的、自发的部分。那恐惧本身就引起他们堵住更多的无意识知识。既然自发性的部分与身体活动是如此相关，他们在促进良好健康上非常重要，而当人们感觉与他们自发的自己分离时，到同样程度，他们也觉得与自己的身体分开了。", "en": "It is only because civilized man has somewhat overspecialized in the use of one kind of knowledge over another that people fear the unconscious, spontaneous portions of the self. The fear alone causes them to block out still more and more unconscious knowledge. Since the spontaneous portions are so related to bodily activity, they are very important in facilitating good health, and when people feel divorced from their spontaneous selves, they also feel divorced to the same extent from their own bodies.", "source": "健康之道 · 第10节", "year": "1984", "tag": null, "short": "健康之道", "session": "10", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0093", "zh": "然而，除了艺术上的自发，任何自发都变得可疑。原因各式各样，在这个讨论里没有必要谈，这个倾向延续到鲁柏的第一任丈夫身上。同时在整个青春期，自我都还没有充分展现出它的真实面目。自发性确实在持续不断的紧张行为以及喜怒无常的行为中爆发了。旁人一直告诉他放慢脚步、要有纪律，而这加深了他害怕他所是，是可怕的、是强大的、是邪恶的恐惧，所以最好藏起来。", "en": "Any spontaneity became suspect however, except artistic spontaneity. For various reasons, not necessary in this discussion, the tendency was carried over with Ruburt's first husband. At the same time through adolescence the quality of the ego had not sufficiently shown its true character as yet. The spontaneity did erupt in constant nervous behavior, and erratic behavior. He was constantly told to slow down, to use discipline, and this reinforced the fear that what he was, was fearful, powerful, evil, and best hidden.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第320节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "320", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0120", "zh": "就连听他念诗的修女也不信任他的热情，并且批评他，他们不相信那种天马行空的事情。如你所知，由于别人对他警告过可能产生的可怕后果，所以他就被自己本性里的自发性给吓坏了。", "en": "Even the nuns to whom he read poetry distrusted his fervency, and took him to task. They distrusted the dramatic quality. The spontaneous elements of his nature, as you know, frightened him, since others gave him dire warnings as to possible consequences.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第421节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "421", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0130", "zh": "如你所知，在情绪高涨的情况下，他母亲告诉他，他可能会精神错乱，因此他不管自己强烈的自发行动是属于什么性质，都会与这件事连结在一起。举例来说：他就曾经发现，高速行驶汽车令人心惊肉跳。现在这些事都让他感到害怕，但是对他来说，任何自发性所带来的都跟高速行驶一样。", "en": "Now he was told under Emotionally charged conditions, as you know, by his mother, that he could or would lose his mind. He tied this in with any strong spontaneous actions on his part, regardless of their nature. An example: once he found it thrilling to ride in an automobile at fast speeds. Now they frighten him. But to him any spontaneity carried the same danger that, say, speeding definitely does.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第421节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "421", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0265", "zh": "自古以来，宗教就试图帮助人了解他自己主观的实相——但宗教有它自己的黑暗面，而为此理由，宗教不幸助长了对自发性的恐惧。", "en": "Since ancient times religion has tried to help man understand the nature of his own subjective reality — but religion has its own dark side, and for this reason religion unfortunately has fostered fear of the spontaneous.", "source": "健康之道 · 第10节", "year": "1984", "tag": null, "short": "健康之道", "session": "10", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0221", "zh": "（“宗教与科学两者都是建立在这种信念上。任何“自发的”发生的事都被投以怀疑的眼光。那个字仿佛暗示那些失控的成分，或从一个极端到另一个极端的移动。看起来好像理性心智才有任何像秩序、纪律或控制这类的概念。因此，人在他自己的心智里就注定了与他的天性作对，而他认为他必须控制它。但事实是，人的意识的确能变得觉察——觉察那些自发性的过程。但他自己已大半关闭了理解之门，因此，他只与他所认为的理性认同，而尽可能的试着忘记心智如此得意洋洋的骑于其上的那些自发性过程。”", "en": "“Man is therefore set against his nature in his own mind, and he thinks he must control it. The fact is that man’s consciousness can indeed become aware of — aware of — those spontaneous processes. But he himself has largely closed the door of comprehension, so that he only identifies with what he thinks of as his rational mind, and tries to forget as best he can those spontaneous processes upon which the mind rides so triumphantly. “He has often become frightened of his own creativity, then, since he has not trusted its source.”", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第845节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "845", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0267", "zh": "在这种社会里的人们，往往受到营养不良、频繁挨揍、灌肠剂的过度使用，及常常过度施行体罚之苦。儿童被严格地管教，而欠缺正常的自发性成了常规而非例外。这种组织的成员往往得了他们身体无法运用营养的病。他们常趋附某种时尚食物，但由于真的害怕自发性到如此的程度，他们往往变得罹患了与身体的无意识过程相关的疾病。", "en": "People in such societies often suffer from malnourishment, frequent beatings, an excessive use of the enema, and often indulge in physical punishment. The children are strictly raised, and a lack of normal spontaneity is the rule rather than the exception. Members of such organizations often suffer maladies in which their bodies do not utilize nutrients. They are often food faddists of one kind or another, but because they do fear spontaneity to such a degree they will often become afflicted with diseases or maladies associated with the body’s unconscious processes.", "source": "健康之道 · 第10节", "year": "1984", "tag": null, "short": "健康之道", "session": "10", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0178", "zh": "他的死板阻止了任何真正伟大的宗教性释放所必须的自发性。他反而跌入了乡土主义的陷阱。如果他扮演好了那个可能的角色，他可以有助于保罗。他是基督存有里的保罗部分的一个可能人格。", "en": "His rigidity prevented the spontaneity necessary for any true great religious release. He fell, instead, into the trap of provincialism. Had he performed the role possible, he could have been of benefit to Paul. He was a probable personality of the Paul portion of the Christ entity.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第588节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "588", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0202", "zh": "习俗之存在是有很好的理由的。一般的说，它们有助于组织经验。如果它们被轻松的执持及接受的话，它们很可以作为指导原则。但被严格奉行的话，它们就变成了不必要的教条，僵化的限制了经验。这同时适用于内在与外在活动。习俗是阶层化及僵化的“自发性”结果。一度，以你们的说法，每个风俗都有一个意义，每一个代表了一个自发的姿势，一个个人化的反应。可是，当这些变成了一个制度体系时，那原先的自发性就失去了，而你投射出一个人工的制度，它变得用来分级行为而非表达行为。所以，有心灵的习俗，就如有物质的习俗一样。有宗教与心灵的教材，意识的导游观光，在其中你被告以跟随一条路线或某个节目，你变得害怕私人性的去诠释你发现自己在体验的不论什么实相。", "en": "There are good reasons for conventions. Generally, they help organize experience. If they are lightly held to and accepted, they can serve well as guidelines. Applied with a heavy hand they become unnecessary dogma, rigidly limiting experience. This applies to inner and outer activity. Conventions are the results of stratified and rigid “spontaneity.” At one time, in your terms, each custom had a meaning. Each represented a spontaneous gesture, an individual reaction. When these become a system of order, however, the original spontaneity is lost, and you project an artificial order that serves to stratify behavior rather than to express it. So there are psychic customs as there are physical ones, religious and psychic dogmas, guided tours of consciousness in which you are told to follow a certain line or a certain program. You become afraid of your private interpretation of whatever reality you find yourself experiencing.", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第714节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "714", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B06", "title": "自发性的自己不会背叛你：你的安全就在自发性里", "note": "这一节翻掉「不管好就会出事」的直觉。赛斯对鲁柏的诊断是：他的病、他的症状，大半是对自发性的恐惧造的压制——而你越怕它越要管它，能量就越堵。他给出的方向是：尽可能撤销限制，自发性的自己相当有弹性，犯了错会自己修正回来；你的安全确实就在自发性里，只有信任它的时候才是真正安全。对你们两人这类人格，宁可往自发那一侧多错一点，也别过度克制——过度克制会真的让能力失灵。信任你自己存在的自发性，你之内没有任何事值得害怕。", "src": "第 314、344、405、422、677、732、617 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 314 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 344 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 405 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 422 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 677 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 732 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 617 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-087-e0102", "zh": "尽可能撤销限制。自发性的自己相当有弹性，只是犯了错，就会自己从错误中修正回来。", "en": "Remove as many limitations as possible. The spontaneous self is remarkably resilient, and bounces back from its own errors when it makes any.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第344节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "344", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0115", "zh": "他不必害怕自己自发性的自己，这个自己不会背叛他。久未消失的手臂症状代表一种压制因素，心电感应的确存在，存在的生命力远比他想象的要大得多。人真的有天生的防卫力，他不必那么（划线）密切监控自己的念头。", "en": "He need not fear his spontaneous self. It will not betray him. The arm symptoms still hanging on represent an inhibiting factor. Telepathy does exist, but existence has a far greater vitality than he supposes. People do have a natural defense. He does not need to watch his thoughts that (underlined) closely.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第405节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "405", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0138", "zh": "你也可以帮忙，提醒他：他的安全确实就在自发性里，而任何完全而突然的释放都会带来喜悦。过去他不愿接受他自发的天性，因为他觉得自己不够自律、不够强壮，控制不了它，而且他不愿为它承担责任。", "en": "You can also help by reminding him that his safety does lie in spontaneity, and that joy will result from any complete and sudden release. In the past he did not want to accept his spontaneous nature because he felt he was not sufficiently disciplined or strong enough to control it, and he did not want to accept the responsibility for it.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第422节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "422", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0136", "zh": "在他的例子里，他做了一些改变，严重地阻碍了自发性在身体动作上的表达。在某种程度上，这是为了让自己安心。当他明白——你可以帮他——他只有在信任自己的自发性时才真正安全，那时他就会自由。", "en": "In his case he made alterations that severely prevented expression of spontaneity, in physical movement. To some extent this was meant to reassure him. When he realizes, and you can help him, that he is indeed safe, only when he trusts his spontaneity, then he will be free.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第422节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "422", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0191", "zh": "如果有任何人告诉你，因为你的天性或肉身的存在，你是邪恶的或有罪的，或任何这类教条，不要信任他。不要信任任何领你离开自己真实的人，（长久停顿，双眼闭着）不要追随那些告诉你必须赎罪——不论以什么方式——的人。相反的，信任你自己存在的自发性，以及为你自己拥有的那个生活。如果你不喜欢你在的地方，那么就检查你的那些信念，把它们带到光天化日之下。在你之内没有任何事值得害怕。", "en": "(Pause at 11:00.) Trust no person who tells you that you are evil or guilty by reason of your nature or your physical existence, or any such dogma. Trust no one who leads you away from the reality of yourself. (Long pause, eyes closed.) Do not follow those who tell you that you must do penance, in whatever form. Trust instead the spontaneity of your own being and the life that is your own. If you do not like where you are, then examine those beliefs that you have. Bring them out into the open. There is nothing within yourself to fear.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第677节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "677", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0088", "zh": "如果你犯了错，有鉴于你们的人格特质，比起过度克制，在自发方面犯错的危险性低很多。过度克制最终可能造成能力无法施展。过度自发最糟不过就是产生一些尴尬的时刻而已。我只是在讲你们的个人情况而已。能力有使用就会有增长。这再怎么强调都不为过。", "en": "Now, if you err, it is far less dangerous to err on the side of spontaneity, given your personalities, than it is to use too much restraint. Too much restraint could eventually make the abilities inoperable. Too much spontaneity at worst could only cause some embarrassing moments. I am speaking of your personal cases only. The ability grows as it is used. This cannot be stressed too highly.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第314节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "314", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0091", "zh": "你看，随着鲁柏允许它自己自发，再一次，他对母亲的认同将会自动消失，它引发的症状也会解除。给你们两位我最好的祝福，而且我时不时会来照看你们一下。睡前给自己建设性的暗示特别重要，并且要求自己做疗愈梦，因为这些会自动缓解早晨的症状，进一步驱散他对母亲挥之不去的认同。", "en": "You see, as Ruburt allows himself spontaneity, again, the mother identification will automatically vanish, and with it the symptoms it causes. My best wishes to you both and I shall look in on you now and then. The constructive suggestions before bed are particularly important, and the request for therapeutic dreams, as these automatically relieve the morning symptoms, and further dissipate the lingering mother identification.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第318节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "318", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0268", "zh": "“放下”是信任你自己存在的自发性，信任你自己的能量、权力与力量，并对你自己生命的能量投降（abandon）。“投降”这字本身可能冲击一些读者为特别的强烈，但自然的每个元素都对那生命形式投降。你身体的每个原子也一样。那么，对你自己生命的力量投降，是依赖诞生出宇宙和你，在大自然内却超越大自然的伟大力量。", "en": "To “let go” is to trust the spontaneity of your own being, to trust your own energy and power and strength, and to abandon yourself to the energy of your own life. The word “abandon” itself may strike some readers as particularly strong, but each element of nature abandons itself to the lifeform. So does each atom of your body. To abandon yourself, then, to the power of your own life, is to rely upon the great forces within and yet beyond nature that gave birth to the universe and to you.", "source": "健康之道 · 第11节", "year": "1984", "tag": null, "short": "健康之道", "session": "11", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0269", "zh": "求生的意志也天生在自然的每个元素里，而如果你信任自己的自发性，那么“存在的意志”便经由你所有的活动而喜悦地释放与表达。它也十分真实地洗掉沮丧和自杀的倾向。", "en": "(Long pause at 3:26.) The will to live is also inbred into each element of nature, and if you trust your own spontaneity, then that will to be is joyfully released and expressed through all of your activities. It can also quite literally wash depression and suicidal tendencies away.", "source": "健康之道 · 第11节", "year": "1984", "tag": null, "short": "健康之道", "session": "11", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0104", "zh": "你要知道，其中一个症状就是害怕他自己的自发性。", "en": "One of the symptoms, you understand, is a fear of his own spontaneity.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第344节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "344", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0035", "zh": "本体，实际上，既是自我也是内我，但更为偏向内我。这以前就提过了，但鲁柏在早年变得这么害怕他自己的自发性，以至于出于恐惧，他或多或少被迫否认他认同内我这件事是对的。在某些情况下，就像前天晚上那样，他自发地接受这份认同，尤其是在酒精发挥抗忧郁作用的时候。", "en": "The identity, indeed, is as much and more the inner self as it is the ego. This has been mentioned in the past, but Ruburt became so fearful of his own spontaneity in early life that he was more or less forced, out of fear, to deny the validity of his identity with the inner self. On some occasions, as the other evening, he spontaneously accepts this identification, particularly when alcohol acts as a depressant.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第132节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "132", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0089", "zh": "他最初在几年前发展出这种客观的态度，是因为他害怕他无法控制他自己的自发。然而，它却增长成太过强大的盔甲，使得他有窒息之处。现在上课时他不再阻挡资料，因此我将会有一个更加自由的声音，可以在需要的时候找你商量。", "en": "He developed this objective manner originally years ago because he feared he could not control his own spontaneity. It grew, however, into too strong an armor, and threatened to suffocate him. He will no longer block material now in the sessions, and therefore I will have a freer voice to counsel you when it may be needed.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第317节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "317", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0141", "zh": "在某些灵性治疗的案例里，信念并不必要。在鲁柏的情形里，信与不信本身就是问题的一部分。因此信念是必要的，因为对自发性的不信、对自发性的恐惧，正是这个困难的一个基本成因。", "en": "In some cases of spiritual healing, belief is not necessary. In Ruburt’s case belief and unbelief were part of the problem itself. Belief therefore was necessary, for unbelief of spontaneity, fear of spontaneity, was a basic cause of the difficulty-....", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第424节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "424", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0185", "zh": "那么，你就要相信你天生是个不受限制的生灵，生成肉身，为的是尽你所能地把本性中伟大的喜悦和自发性，具体地显现出来。", "en": "Believe, then, that you are a being unlimited by nature, born into flesh to materialize as best you can the great joy and spontaneity of your nature.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第617节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "617", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B07", "title": "创造诞生于游戏，不诞生于苦功", "note": "赛斯有一句宣言式的断言：所有创造与意识都诞生于游戏的特性而非工作的特性，诞生于加快了的直觉性自发性。他拿自己前世举例——当那个在午后玩球的「轻佻女子」那一世，对自发与喜悦之本性的了悟胜过许多沉重的知性生涯。所以他要鲁柏（和每个人）在工作时段允许自发的空间，记得童年的自发，像想一朵花的自由那样想自己的创造力。疗愈也走同一条路：任何形式的游戏都鼓励自发性、促进疗愈，给意识心一个不再担忧的休息。", "src": "第 58、97、483、514、515、518、521、891 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 58 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 97 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 483 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 514 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 515 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 518 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 521 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 891 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-087-e0169", "zh": "我们开始学到“游戏”的创造性喜悦。例如，我相信所有的创造与意识是诞生于游戏的特性而非工作的特性，诞生于加快了的直觉性的自发性中，在我自己所有的存在中，以及我所知的别人的经验中这都是不变的常态。", "en": "We are beginning to learn the creative joy of play. I believe, for example, that all creativity and consciousness is born in the quality of play, as opposed to work, in the quickened intuitional spontaneity that I see as a constant through all my own existences, and in the experience of those I know.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第518节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "518", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0171", "zh": "因此它创造种种不同的情况而在其中运作，并给自己设下挑战，有些挑战在你们来说一定会遭失败，至少在一开始是如此，因为它首先必须创造那些会带来新创造的情况。而所有这些它都是怀着伟大的自发性与无限的喜悦来做的。（停顿）", "en": "Therefore it creates varieties of conditions in which to operate, and sets itself challenges, some doomed to failure in your terms, at least initially, because it must first create the conditions which will bring new creations about. And all of this is done with great spontaneity and unbounded joy. (Pause.)", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第521节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "521", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0161", "zh": "现在。在我的许多前世里，我当过知识分子式的绅士，也当过轻佻的女子。然而我要告诉你们：作为那个轻佻女子——爱在明媚的午后玩球，没有杂务要做——看似游手好闲，看似一个全然无用的人格……我倒不曾被知性所累……可偏偏就在那一世里，我对自发与喜悦之本性的了悟，胜过我那许多沉重的知性生涯。", "en": "Now. I have been in my many pasts an intellectual gentleman and a frivolous female. And yet I will tell you, that as a frivolous female who loved to play with a ball in the bright afternoon and had no chores to perform, seemingly an idle life and seemingly a quite useless personality.... I was not burdened with intellect... and yet in that one particular life I learned more about the nature of spontaneity and joy than in many of my ponderous intellectual existences.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第483节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "483", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0160", "zh": "你们每天必须试着腾出一段时间，忘掉你们自认为是的那个自己……成年人的装腔作势，成年人的了不得。你们必须记得童年的自发性。你们必须去想一朵花里面的自由。在你们看来，花不会动，因而没有自由。然而我告诉你们，你们必须思考一朵花的自由。", "en": "You must try to forget for a period of time each day the self that you think of as yourself... the adult pretensions, the adult bigness’s. You must remember the childhood spontaneity. You must think of the freedom that is within a flower. Now it seems to you that a flower cannot move, and therefore has no freedom. And yet I tell you, you must think about the freedom of a flower.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第483节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "483", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0253", "zh": "在其它的儿童病例里，叫孩子玩一个治愈游戏，在其中，他好玩地想象他又再是完全健康地于户外游戏；或叫那小孩想象和一个朋友在谈话，描写那疾病为已过去了。甚至在老人院里，也可用游戏，因为它可以令自发的感觉复苏，给意识心一个休息而不再担忧。", "en": "In other cases of a child’s illness, have the child play a healing game, in which he or she playfully imagines being completely healthy again, outdoors and playing; or have the youngster imagine a conversation with a friend, describing the illness as past and gone. Play could also be used even in old peoples’ homes, for it could revive feelings of spontaneity and give the conscious mind a rest from worrying.", "source": "健康之道 · 第7节", "year": "1984", "tag": null, "short": "健康之道", "session": "7", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0254", "zh": "在所有种种的疾病里，只要可能的时候，且以不论什么方式，游戏都该被培养。许多独裁性的宗教根本尖锐地拒绝容许他们的信众沉迷于任何一种游戏，而不悦地视之为罪恶。纸牌游戏和家庭游戏——像“大富翁”，实际上是极佳的练习，而任何形式的游戏都鼓励自发性，并促进疗愈及平静。", "en": "In all cases of illness, games or play should be fostered whenever possible, and in whatever form. Many dictatorial religions pointedly refuse to allow their congregations to indulge in any type of play at all, and frown upon it as sinful. Card-playing and family games such as Monopoly are actually excellent practices, and play in any form encourages spontaneity and promotes healing and peace of mind.", "source": "健康之道 · 第7节", "year": "1984", "tag": null, "short": "健康之道", "session": "7", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0025", "zh": "他这样惩罚自己很可笑，对事情也没有帮助，因为在他的工作习惯中，喜悦的自发太重要了。", "en": "It is ridiculous for him to so punish himself, and does not help matters, as his joyous spontaneity is so important in his working habits.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第97节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "97", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0017", "zh": "你将会帮忙在人们心中创造他们在看见你的作品之前没有的东西。这是你的承诺。现在正是时候。如果你要像你选择的那样成为一个存有，那这就是你的机会，这是你在这个地球最后一次转世。在创作的时候，你需要力量、实力、决心以及喜悦的自发。", "en": "You will help to create something in the hearts of men that will not be there until they see your work. This is your commitment. This is the time for it. If you are to be an entity, as you have chosen to be, then this is your opportunity, and this is your last reincarnation upon this earth. You need power, strength, determination, and joyous spontaneity in your working hours.", "source": "早期课第2册 · 第58节", "year": "1964", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第2册", "session": "58", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0139", "zh": "我们还有一项注。鲁柏自发的天性是宽容的、明朗的，按他自己的标准来说是相当天生的善良——当他否认自发性而试图制造这些特质时，便觉得它们如此困难。我现在期待一个明确的好转，而鲁柏一准备好，我们就会开始我的书。", "en": "We have one further note. Ruburt’s spontaneous nature is tolerant, sunny, quite natively good in his terms—qualities that he finds so difficult when he tries to manufacture them while denying spontaneity. I expect now a definite change for the better, and as soon as Ruburt is ready, then we will begin my book.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第422节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "422", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0168", "zh": "你们经常在改变你们的肉体及最密切的环境的形相、形状、轮廓与意义，虽然你们尽量忽略这些经常不断的变化。相反的，我们容许它们完全的自由，因为我们知道我们被一个“内在的稳定”所策动，它当得起自发性与创造性，并且悟到心灵的和心理的身份感是依赖着创造性的改变。", "en": "You are constantly changing the form, the shape, the contour, and the meaning of your physical body and most intimate environment, although you do your best to ignore these constant alterations. On the other hand, we allow them full rein, knowing that we are motivated by an inner stability that can well afford spontaneity and creation, and realizing that spiritual and psychological identity are dependent upon creative change.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第514节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "514", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0180", "zh": "意识是自然而然、自发性的在创造。在三度空间中，你们学习各种以情感及心灵创造不同物质形相的方法。你们在心灵的环境中操作，操作的结果立即印映在成形的物质上。而我们的环境却本身即具有创造力，这是与你们的环境大不相同的地方。你们环境中的创造力显示于树可以开花结果上，这中间有着自足的原则，譬如说大地可以自给自足，而这种创作的面貌则是你们最深层的心灵、精神及人类的性向，经过物质化而呈现于你们这个世界中的结果。这些全是久远前就预定的，取自人类心灵知识库中部分资料。", "en": "Consciousness is, among other things, a spontaneous exercise in creativity. You are learning now, in a three-dimensional context, the ways in which your emotional and psychic existence can create varieties of physical form. You manipulate within the psychic environment, and these manipulations are then automatically impressed upon the physical mold. Now our environment is in itself creative in a different manner than yours. Your environment is creative in that trees bear fruit, that there is a self-sustaining principle, that the earth feeds its own, for example. The naturally creative aspects are the materializations of the deepest psychic, spiritual, and physical inclinations of the species, set up in your terms eons ago, and a part of the racial bank of psychic knowledge.", "source": "时空之外 · 第515节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "时空之外", "session": "515", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0230", "zh": "（“三：我要记住我生存于其中的“存在的创造性构架”。因此，构架二的可能性、潜能、看似奇迹的事及快乐的自发性将在我心中，而因此‘创造性的生活’之门打开了。", "en": "“Three: I will remember the creative framework of existence, in which I have my being. Therefore the possibilities, potentials, seeming miracles, and joyful spontaneity of Framework 2 will be in my mind, so that the doors to creative living are open.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第891节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "891", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B08", "title": "要证据、要灵感，只能自发地来", "note": "赛斯对灵媒工作、对实验室、对 ESP 训练给的操作性建议全是同一句话：自发性是前提条件。他说过只有自发性才真的给我们任何结果；如果太关注效果，自发就消失，自我进来，就全完了。这也是他解释「为什么实验室里拿不到永存的证据」：那种气氛不允许自发性。落到练习上：你越用力试，越会挡掉资料与身体的自发移动；当你忘掉实验这回事，就做得非常好。对内在感官迈出的「自发性的第一步」，才是意识心不得不接受的证据的来源。", "src": "第 25、103、169、170、172、178、179、205、573、744 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 25 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 103 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 169 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 170 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 172 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 178 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 179 节"}, {"n": 8, "id": null, "label": "第 205 节"}, {"n": 9, "id": null, "label": "第 573 节"}, {"n": 10, "id": null, "label": "第 744 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-087-e0002", "zh": "这并不意味着不能发现，内在感官确实存在的证据和压倒性证据。它的确意味着必须允许自发性的存在。要找到内在感官收到的资料与外在感官感受到的资料之间有何关联，是极端困难的。", "en": "This does not mean that evidence cannot be found, and overwhelming evidence, for the existence of the inner senses. It does mean that spontaneity must be allowed for. It is extremely difficult to relate data received by the inner senses into data that will be picked up by the outer senses.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第25节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "25", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0003", "zh": "事实是，当你坚持要透过外在的、公认的感官接受证据时，你几乎就自动地关闭了内在感官装置。这是没有必要的。这样的习惯性反应在很大程度上是人自己设定的。这不是一个自然的习惯反应。你必须接受内在资料的千真万确，但你不会这样做。一旦你迈开这自发性的第一步，你就真的会收到、甚至是你的意识心也不得不接受的证据。但是，你必须先有这样的意愿踏出第一步。", "en": "The fact is that when you insist upon evidence through the outside, regularly accepted senses, that you almost automatically turn off the inner sense apparatus. This is not necessary. Man to a large degree has set up this habit reaction. It is not a natural habit reaction. You must take the inner data at its face value, and this is what you will not do. Once you take this first step of spontaneity, you will actually receive evidence that even your conscious mind will be forced to accept. But the first step of such willingness must be made.", "source": "早期课第1册 · 第25节", "year": "1963–64", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第1册", "session": "25", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0056", "zh": "我不会耽误我们的时间。然而，最重要是必须让自发性出来。博士，你所关注的那种证据可以得到。但是，假如我们太过关注效果，那自发性就会消失，自我会进来，我们会迷失……", "en": "I will not keep us. Nevertheless spontaneity must be allowed for primarily. Then the sort of evidence with which you are concerned, Doctor, can be obtained. However, if we are overly concerned for effects then the spontaneity disappears. The ego comes in and we are lost....", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第169节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "169", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0060", "zh": "不会看的人，他们就是不会看。我会尽我所能。不过，这样的效果在我们极为平常的上课中间就会呈现出来。再说一次，只有自发性才真的会给我们任何的结果。", "en": "Those who will not see, they will not see. I will do my best. However, such effects will appear in the middle of quite ordinary sessions. For again, only spontaneity will give us any results at all.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第170节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "170", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0061", "zh": "为什么过去一直找不到永存不灭（immorality）的充分证据，其原因很多。别的原因先不提，光是实验室的实验和气氛就脱不了关系，因为在其中不允许自发性。", "en": "There are many reasons why adequate proofs for immortality have not been received in the past. These reasons have to do, among other things, with the laboratory experiments and atmosphere, which do not allow for spontaneity.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第170节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "170", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0062", "zh": "任何要展现的效果，都只会在一般平时的课中出现。我会确实努力让那些效果尽量明确、清楚，以符合需求。不过，在任何这类的展现中，自发性都会是先决条件。", "en": "Any effects that are demonstrated will appear within ordinary sessions. I will endeavor indeed to see that they are as definite as possible, and as clear-cut as will be desired. But spontaneity will as always remain a prerequisite for any such displays.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第172节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "172", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0065", "zh": "我并没有意愿设定任何不合理或不可能的条件。不过，一种信任、互相信任的气氛似乎不可或缺。同时也必须允许自发性的表现。", "en": "First of all, I have no information of setting up any unreasonable nor impossible conditions. An atmosphere of trust, mutual trust, would however seem to be indispensable. Spontaneity must be allowed for.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第179节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "179", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0072", "zh": "在这里如果你不喜欢用情绪（emotions）这个字眼，或许可以用活力（vitality）来取代。殷斯翠姆博士，我个人很感谢你对我们的兴趣，你们会成功的。再次的，如果可能，不要一直专注在理智的层面。当鲁柏太努力去尝试，他反而会因为推动了自发性而阻挡了资料；当你试得太努力，会打断所有的交流，至少会把它变得比较困难。", "en": "If you dislike the term emotions in this context, the word vitality may be substituted. I personally appreciate your interest, Dr. Instream, and we shall indeed succeed. Again, do not concentrate on an intellectual level, if possible. When Ruburt tries too hard, he often blocks material by losing spontaneity; and when you try too hard, you interrupt any communication, or at least make it more difficult.", "source": "早期课第5册 · 第205节", "year": "1966", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第5册", "session": "205", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0064", "zh": "他的本性在许多方面会以自然的方式流露出极端的自发性，这一项特质对我们很重要。我们真的会利用各种机会来做测试，我们的成果将相当依赖鲁柏的能力发展和自信心。这极其自然，他自己实验得太辛苦了，当他忘掉实验这回事，就做得非常好。", "en": "In many ways his nature is extremely spontaneous in a natural fashion, and it is this attribute that is important to us. We will indeed try our own tests on various occasions. Our results will depend to a large degree upon the development of Ruburt’s abilities, and upon his own confidence. This is quite natural. He tries too hard with his own tests. When he forgets to try he does very well.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第178节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "178", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0059", "zh": "亲爱的殷斯翠姆博士，对于我会透过哪一种人格来讲话，你或许多少有些兴趣。我要的人格必须同时兼具理性与直觉，我要的自我是能平衡得很好，很健康、很强壮。还有，我要的人格必须能够允许它自己必然的自发行为与内在自由，以便这一类的沟通可以发生。没有基本稳定度的人格不符合我的目标需求，在信仰上和能力上太过僵化的人格，也不太符合我的目标需求。", "en": "All right now. You may be interested to some degree, dear Doctor Instream, in the sort of personality through whom I speak. I wanted a personality who was at the same time both intelligent and intuitional. I wanted an ego which was well balanced, healthy and strong. Yet I also wanted a personality which would allow itself the spontaneity necessary, and the inner freedom, so that such communications could take place. A personality without basic stability would not serve my purposes, and a personality that was too rigid in its beliefs and abilities would not serve my purposes well.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第170节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "170", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0029", "zh": "当然，状况有利的话，这样的课可以让我们利用活动高峰，增强我们的自发性。而且有了增强的自发性，我们就会减轻任何扭曲效应。这些效应很少发生，除了在私人资料中，或在鲁柏因为怀疑而感觉有压力的情况下。在心灵活动的高峰中，怀疑会减到最低。", "en": "Naturally, conditions being beneficial, such sessions may allow us to take advantage of high peaks of activity and increase our spontaneity. And with increased spontaneity we will decrease any distortive effects. These effects very rarely occur, except in personal material, or in cases where Ruburt feels under pressure because of doubts. During high peaks of psychic activity the doubts are minimized.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第103节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "103", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0175", "zh": "因为它处于这样的境地，它在操纵人体上又有些特别的用处。当你们正在学的时候，自发性在此是极端重要的。你在进入阿尔法状态之前的意识大半决定你将有那种经验，它自动地把你的注意力集中于那些特殊区域。", "en": "Because it is so situated, it is also of particular use in manipulating the physical organism. As you are learning, spontaneity is extremely important here. Your intent before you enter the alpha state largely predetermines the kind of experience you will have, automatically focusing your attention in those specified areas.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第573节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "573", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0066", "zh": "我的确说的相当明白，在任何这类彼此诚实对待的努力中，我都愿意合作，也会付诸行动，我在谈到条件，说要符合我的条件时，再重早一次，我不会开出任何不可能达成的条件；我只说自发性、信任和诚实是我们努力过程中的必备要素。", "en": "I did say quite plainly that I would cooperate in any such endeavor that is conducted with integrity, and so I shall. When I spoke of terms, saying that my terms should be met, I was not, again, speaking of any impossible conditions; merely that spontaneity, trust and integrity be necessary factors in our endeavor.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第179节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "179", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0212", "zh": "在这些课里，如你们了解的脑波之全部范围都被用上了。在此，在一个非常具创造性、有纪律却又自发性的表现里，一个情况被设定了，在其中已知的频率组合了起来，所以意识能更完全的用它自己，达到许多对一个意识范围所关闭的领域，而获得知识。“觉察”的每个层面之种种不同而独特的特性都被给予了施展的机会。以一种说法，这是像一个加速的、选好的、组织良好的“有意识的”梦冒险，在其中鲁柏旅游过意识的媒介，直到最后他，仍然是他自己，然而又不再是他自己（幽默的），却是我。", "en": "In these sessions the full range of brain waves is utilized as you understand them. Here, in a highly creative, disciplined, and yet spontaneous performance, a situation is set up in which knowledge is obtained from the known frequencies, combined so that consciousness can use itself more fully, reaching into many areas closed to one range of consciousness alone. The various diverse, unique characteristics of each level of awareness are given play. In a way this is like an accelerated, chosen, well-organized “conscious” dream venture, in which Ruburt travels through mediums of consciousness until finally he, still being himself, is nevertheless no longer himself (humorously), but me.", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第744节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "744", "only_en": false}]}]}, {"id": "B09", "title": "情感的自发：能量天生会自己流出去", "note": "赛斯把自发性接到情绪上，正好翻转「先控制情绪」的通识：情感本身的设计就是自然控制、并且有助纪律的装置，因为它们允许能量自发地向外流动；唯有情感受到否定，才会爆炸、怒吼、生病。所以感觉的自发性几乎会自动给你更大的自由，促进身心健康；他说要打开很多扇门，说的就是情感的自发性。顺带一句常被忽略的：你不干涉自己的时候，本来就是自发地讲理的——理性和自发看起来不对盘，是你自己的信念造成的假象。", "src": "第 151、152、160、616、617、667、857 节", "cites": [{"n": 1, "id": null, "label": "第 151 节"}, {"n": 2, "id": null, "label": "第 152 节"}, {"n": 3, "id": null, "label": "第 160 节"}, {"n": 4, "id": null, "label": "第 616 节"}, {"n": 5, "id": null, "label": "第 617 节"}, {"n": 6, "id": null, "label": "第 667 节"}, {"n": 7, "id": null, "label": "第 857 节"}], "groups": [{"label": "", "note": null, "picks": [{"id": "q-concept-087-e0044", "zh": "如果你将全部的感受力都导向忧虑的觉受，那么无论如何平衡就有问题。感觉的自发性几乎都会自动给你更大的自由，促进身心健康，进而维持良好的平衡。", "en": "When all your sensitivity is directed into sensations of misgiving, then however the balance is wrong. Spontaneity of feeling will almost automatically allow you greater freedom, increased mental and physical health; and balance will then be very well maintained.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第151节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "151", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0045", "zh": "我告诉你们，你们真的是朝向更舒适的阶段迈进，但这并不是说你们现在的日常生活没有什么值得感恩的事。自发性将会打开很多扇门，我说的是情感的自发性。", "en": "I tell you that you are indeed headed for more comfortable times, but this does not mean that there is not very much within your own daily life now to be thankful for. Spontaneity will open many doors. I am speaking of emotional spontaneity.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第151节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "151", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0046", "zh": "这并不是说人格一定要完全被一种情感席卷，但自我怕的就是这样。情感甚至为自我补充能量。情感必须有弹性，而弹性既是自发性，也是内在的确信以及纪律的结果。所有这一切都是行动，因为人格本身就是由行动组成，而且持续不断变化。因此，这是个乐见自我表达和形式的行动。", "en": "This does not mean that the personality must be completely swept away by an emotion, though this is what such an ego fears. Emotion replenishes even the ego. Emotions demand resiliency, and resiliency is both the result of spontaneity, inner assurance, and discipline. All this is action, for the personality itself is composed of action, and is constantly changing. This is action, therefore, delighting in the expression and form of itself.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第152节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "152", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0052", "zh": "就是由于自我被误导，才会企图跳脱情感，寻求稳定，使得自我采取这样的回应方式。它害怕失去控制、失去纪律，但事实完全相反。情感本身的设计，就是可以自然控制，而且有助于纪律，因为它们允许能量自发性地向外流动。唯有情感受到否定时，才具有爆炸性或对人格造成危险，然后才真的会导致猛爆攻击、怒吼咆哮、身心疾病，以及各种不幸的遭遇。", "en": "It is, again, the ego's misguided attempt to stand apart to gain stability, that makes the ego react in such a manner. It fears loss of control and of discipline. But all appearances to the contrary, the emotions are natural controlling devices that in themselves aid discipline, since they allow for the spontaneous flow of energies outward. It is only when they are denied that they become explosive or dangerous to the personality. Then indeed they result in explosive barrages, ranting and shouting, organic and psychological illnesses, and of unfortunate manifestations.", "source": "早期课第4册 · 第160节", "year": "1965", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第4册", "session": "160", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0183", "zh": "因此，限制性的意念自动就会令你去接受那些类似的观念。同样的，那些洋溢着自由、愉悦与自发性的意念，也自动地把同类的想法吸了过去。人与人之间有着无休止的相互作用，其中充满了各种念头的交换，包括了意识上与心电感应上的。", "en": "Limiting ideas therefore predispose you to accept others of a similar nature. Exuberant ideas of freedom, spontaneity and joy automatically collect others of their kind also. There is a constant interplay between yourself and others in the exchange of ideas, both telepathically and on a conscious level.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第616节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "616", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0184", "zh": "如我以前提到的（在第六一六节里），你也不停地放出自己的心电感应思想。别人也就根据他们自己对实相的意念而作出反应。借着把注意力集中在生机、力量与创造性的念头上，一个家庭能不断地加强它的喜悦（较大声地）、欢乐和自发性；或者借着加强怨恨、愤怒、怀疑与失败的想法，（较低沉地）也可以让它一半的能量白白溜走。", "en": "As I mentioned earlier (in the 616th session), you are also sending your own telepathic thoughts outward. Others will react to those according to their own ideas of reality. A family can constantly reinforce its joy (louder), gaiety, and spontaneity by concentrating on ideas of vitality, strength and creativity; or it can let half of its energy slip away (deeper) by reinforcing resentments, angers and thoughts of doubt and failure.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第617节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "617", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0189", "zh": "因此，非常聪明的父母也许发现他们生了一个智障儿。如果他们把很大的价值放在知性上，而牺牲了情感，那么这个小孩也许会为他们演出自己最怕的情感自发性。", "en": "Highly intelligent parents, therefore, may find themselves with a retarded child. If they place a great value upon intellect at the expense of the emotions, then the child may be acting out for them the emotional spontaneity of which they are so afraid themselves.", "source": "个人实相的本质 · 第667节", "year": "1972–73", "tag": null, "short": "个人实相的本质", "session": "667", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0224", "zh": "当你不干涉自己的时候，你是自发的讲理的，但因为你的信念使得理性与自发性看起来好像是不相亲的伴侣。", "en": "When you let yourselves alone, you are spontaneously reasonable, but because of your beliefs it seems that reason and spontaneity make poor bedfellows.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第857节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "857", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0262", "zh": "有些人可能很难相信，自发性是该被信任的，因为他们可能只觉察破坏性或暴力的冲动感觉。自发地表达冲动的概念，在那种情况下，将是最令人恐怖的。", "en": "It will be difficult for some people to believe that spontaneity is to be trusted, for they may be only aware of feeling destructive or violent impulses. The idea of expressing impulses spontaneously will be most frightening under those conditions.", "source": "健康之道 · 第10节", "year": "1984", "tag": null, "short": "健康之道", "session": "10", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0242", "zh": "这节结束。再次的，我要给我们的朋友一个备忘录——要信任形成他自己影像的宇宙之伟大力量，要信任他的自发性，以及他身体想要放松、移动和创造的自然冲动，当它们以它们自己的节奏显示自己时。", "en": "End of session. A small note to our friend — again — to trust the great power of the universe that forms his own image, to trust his spontaneity, and his body’s natural urges toward relaxation, motion, and creativity, as these show themselves in their own rhythms.", "source": "神奇之道 · 第17节", "year": "1980", "tag": null, "short": "神奇之道", "session": "17", "only_en": false}]}]}], "reading": [{"id": "q-concept-087-e0024", "zh": "菲利普应该读一读特别讲到宇宙法则，也就是宇宙的内在法则那几节，进而体会在所有的宇宙之内的这个宇宙既自发又耐久。重复那个冗长的讨论是开倒车，但是，就像内在宇宙有自发和耐久的属性，就像广阔的现在同时存在又涵盖所有的过去和所有的现在以及所有的未来，就像菲利普了解扩展的意义，不在于时间或空间，而在于价值完成，这样他就能凭直觉理解到，当我说宇宙没有开始也没有结束时，与现有的实相没有任何矛盾（contradiction）。（注：重新编译。）", "en": "Philip should read the sessions dealing particularly with the laws of the universe, that is with the inner laws of the universe, appreciating then the facts that this universe within all universes is spontaneous while having durability. It would be backtracking to repeat that long discussion, but as the inner universe has as its attributes spontaneity and durability, and as the spacious present is simultaneous while containing within it all pasts and all presents and all futures, and as Philip understands the meaning of expansion in terms not of time or of space but of value fulfillment, so will he intuitively then grasp that no contradiction occurs with actual reality when I say that there is no beginning and no end.", "source": "早期课第3册 · 第95节", "year": "1964–65", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第3册", "session": "95", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0087", "zh": "当爱猫人和耶稣会士在这里的时候，他阻挡了我几次，那时的状况很适合自发的一节课，说真的，非常适合。我每次都有话要说，但那些时刻一去不复返。他利用身体的病痛当作他自己的借口。身体的病痛从一开始就是抑制。没有自发，他不能有效或顺利地运作。他也读了太多某些方面的东西，而且在一个意识层面太过用力了。", "en": "He has blocked me several times when the cat lover and Jesuit were here, and the circumstances were good for a spontaneous session, particularly good, in fact. I had something to say each time and those moments are gone. He used the physical ailments as excuses to himself. The physical ailments were meant as checks from the beginning. Without spontaneity, he does not operate effectively or well. He has read too, too much along certain lines, and has tried too hard on a conscious level.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第314节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "314", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0095", "zh": "这应该消失，因为他拿回了他自身的自发性，所以这会消失。你比较想要休息或是结束这一节都可以。", "en": "This should vanish, and is as he regains his own spontaneity. You may take a break or end the session as you prefer.", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第320节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "320", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0098", "zh": "他现在开始认同自发的自己是幼儿园的孩子，这是一个明显的进步。你有没有什么特定的问题？", "en": "He is beginning to identify his spontaneous self now with the spontaneity of the nursery school children, and this is a definite improvement. Did you have any specific questions?", "source": "早期课第7册 · 第321节", "year": "1968", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第7册", "session": "321", "only_en": true}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0103", "zh": "只要他处理得不错，就会非常坚强、开放、乐于付出、具有自发性。然而，任何强大的障碍都会使他退缩，尽管面带微笑的个性暂时隐藏了这个事实。", "en": "He is extremely strong, open, and giving and spontaneous when he is functioning well. Any strong impediments cause him to retreat however, though for a while a smiling surface personality hides this fact.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第344节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "344", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0108", "zh": "当他的自发性过度爆发，危险性就少很多。随之而来的困难，如果有的话，会是他在青少年时期遭遇到的那些。然后，你会发现，由于缺乏经验，那些困难变得更严重。他害怕它们，现在反而采取了相反的态势。", "en": "There is far less danger when his spontaneity over erupts. The ensuing difficulties, if any, are those he dealt when as an adolescent. Then they were heightened by lack of experience, you see. He feared them, adopting instead now the opposite tendency.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第346节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "346", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0125", "zh": "他试图让自发与不自发并存。自发性本身有自己的节奏，自然需要一定的休息时间。一旦发生这样子的干扰，就会打乱这些自然节奏。", "en": "He tried to be spontaneous and not spontaneous at the same time. Spontaneity itself has its own rhythm, with needed periods of rest that follow naturally. These natural rhythms are disrupted when such tampering occurs.", "source": "早期课第8册 · 第421节", "year": "1969", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第8册", "session": "421", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0144", "zh": "你对自己否定生命，到头来就是对他人否定生命。我真希望这节课录了音，好让你亲耳听我说——因为我待你如友，紧紧而珍爱，鲁柏[Ruburt]也是如此。但你在某些课里必然会误解我说的话，所以我就更有必要把话说得更直白。你此刻没有觉察——你不肯让自己觉察——你的存在之美，和你之存的繁复的实相。你不肯让自己觉察：你的内我那份自发性与欣喜的迸涌，正是它产生了你称作自己的这个当下的人类人格；也不肯觉察：那投入你的造化的努力与创造的能量，正在你之内歌唱，犹如创世的第一个清晨。", "en": "In denying life to yourself you end up by denying life to others. Now I wish this session was recorded so you could hear me, for I hold you, as Ruburt does, closely and dearly as a friend. But you are bound to misinterpret what I say in some sessions, and so it behooves me to speak more plainly. You do not realize now, you do not let yourself realize, the beauty and the complicated reality of your being. You do not let yourself realize the spontaneity and joyful burst that is your inner self, that results in this present human personality that you call yourself. Nor the effort and creative energy that has gone into your making, and that sings within your being like the first morning of creation.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第440节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "440", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0166", "zh": "那是你所感到的那份生命力的一种流畅（停顿）、灵动的表达。它会带有疗愈的性质。它吸收，却也给予。它显出自发性，是易于流动的那种，而非爆发式的。", "en": "It is a fluid (Pause), mobile expression of the vitality that you sensed. It will have healing qualities. It absorbs, and yet gives. It shows spontaneity, in an easily-moving manner rather than in an explosive way.", "source": "早期课第9册 · 第505节", "year": "1969–70", "tag": null, "short": "早期课第9册", "session": "505", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0177", "zh": "在一方面，人渴望走出他自己之外，走出他的心理存在所居的架构之外，去尝试新的挑战，走出一种意识模式而走入另一种。他想要研究他自己意识的过程。在一方面来说，这意识指远离那给他宁静与安全的“内在自发性”。在另一方面，在他来说这提供给他一种新的创造性。", "en": "Man desired in one way to step out of himself, out of the framework in which he had his psychological existence, to try new challenges, to step out of a mode of consciousness into another. He wanted to study the process of his own consciousness. In one way this meant a giant separation from the inner spontaneity that had given him both peace and security. On the other hand, it offered a new creativity, in his terms.", "source": "灵魂永生 · 第587节", "year": "1970–71", "tag": null, "short": "灵魂永生", "session": "587", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0205", "zh": "威尔梦想着要有自发性。然而，即使在这开放的团体里，对那些够自由去玩味自发性概念，同时却不完全信任它的成人们，班的自发性仍变得令人窘迫。班是害怕知性的，他怕它会把他拉下来。", "en": "Will dreams of being spontaneous. Yet even in this open [class] group, Ben’s spontaneity becomes embarrassing to adults free enough to play with the idea of spontaneity while not trusting it completely. Ben is afraid of the intellect. He is frightened that it will “pull him down.”", "source": "未知的实相卷二 · 第732节", "year": "1974–75", "tag": null, "short": "未知的实相卷二", "session": "732", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0223", "zh": "那么，以较世俗的说法，冲动常常来自无意识的知识。这个知识由组成你身体的能量自动自发的收到，然后再被处理。因此，与你切身有关的资料就可以为你所利用。理想的说，你的冲动总是因应你自己最大的利益反应——并且，也因应你世界的最大利益反应。在当代的世界里，显然有一种对冲动之深而有害的不信赖，而以你们的说法，就你们所知的历史而言也一直是如此。 （停顿）冲动是自发性的，而你会被教以不要去信赖你存在的自发部分却去依赖你的理性与知性——附带说一句（好笑的），那两者的运作却也是十分自发性的！", "en": "In more mundane terms, impulses often come from unconscious knowledge, then. This knowledge is spontaneously and automatically received by the energy that composes your body, and then it is processed so that pertinent information applying to you can be taken advantage of. Ideally (underlined), your impulses are always in response to your own best interests — and, again, to the best interests of your world as well. Obviously there is a deep damaging distrust of impulses in the contemporary world, as in your terms there has been throughout the history that you follow. (Pause.) Impulses are spontaneous, and you have been taught not to trust the spontaneous portions of your being, but to rely upon your reason and your intellect — which (amused) both operate, incidentally, quite spontaneously, by the way.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第857节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "857", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0227", "zh": "你的冲动是你与你的内我最接近的沟通，因为在醒时状态，它们是由你在梦里所有对自己的深层内在知识里升起，而朝向行动的自发性驱策力。（热切的）你生下来是因为你有存在的冲动。宇宙存在，因为它有存在的冲动。并没有外在的宇宙性的彩衣吹笛人（译注：德国传说中的吹笛人，曾以笛音诱使镇上儿童尾随其后，一同隐入山洞而不复见。）唱着魔音或吹着魔调，驱策着宇宙进入存在。想要存在的驱策力是由内而来的，而到某个程度，那股驱策力在人或者分子的每次冲动及每次朝向行动的驱策里都被重复着。如果你不信任你冲动的本质，那么你就不信任你生命的本质，宇宙的本质，或你自己存在的本质。", "en": "Your impulses are your closest communication with your inner self, because in the waking state they are the spontaneous urgings toward action, rising from that deep inner knowledge of yourself that you have in dreams. (Intently:) You were born because you had the impulse to be. The universe exists because it had the impulse to be. There was no exterior cosmic Pied Piper, singing magical notes or playing a magical tune, urging the universe into being. The urge to be came from within, and that urge is repeated to some extent in each impulse, each urge toward action on the part of man or molecule. If you do not trust the nature of your impulses, then you do not trust the nature of your life, the nature of the universe, or the nature of your own being.", "source": "个人与群体事件的本质 · 第870节", "year": "1977–79", "tag": null, "short": "个人与群体事件的本质", "session": "870", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0236", "zh": "当然，你们大多数人想到身体的症状时，你们以一种致命的严肃来看你们的身体，那到某程度阻碍了内在的自发性。你将你局限性的信念置于自然人之上。", "en": "When [most of] you think of physical symptoms, of course, you regard your body with a deadly seriousness that to some extent impedes inner spontaneity. You lay your limiting beliefs upon the natural person.", "source": "梦、进化与价值完成 · 第902节", "year": "1979–82", "tag": null, "short": "梦、进化与价值完成", "session": "902", "only_en": false}, {"id": "q-concept-087-e0272", "zh": "再次的，精神性游戏，插入幽默与消遣，是极端有价值的，以令你不致太过努力。有些人太努力去自发，同时，其它人则害怕自发性本身。对转世生命的知识是自发地持有的，而你能由那知识收到深奥的洞见。这发生在当你并没在寻找它，但却与整个观念够熟悉，因此你觉悟到这种知识是可得的时候。", "en": "Again, mind games, the insertion of humor and diversion, are extremely valuable, so that you are not trying too hard. Some people try too hard to be spontaneous, while others are frightened of spontaneity itself. The knowledge of reincarnational lives is spontaneously held, and you can receive profound insights from that knowledge. This occurs when you are not looking for it, but when you are familiar enough with the entire concept, so that you realize such knowledge is available.", "source": "健康之道 · 第12节", "year": "1984", "tag": null, "short": "健康之道", "session": "12", "only_en": false}], "books": [{"name": "健康之道", "count": 18}, {"name": "早期课第9册", "count": 12}, {"name": "早期课第4册", "count": 12}, {"name": "早期课第2册", "count": 11}, {"name": "早期课第8册", "count": 9}, {"name": "未知的实相卷二", "count": 8}, {"name": "早期课第3册", "count": 7}, {"name": "早期课第7册", "count": 7}, {"name": "早期课第1册", "count": 6}, {"name": "个人与群体事件的本质", "count": 6}, {"name": "个人实相的本质", "count": 6}, {"name": "灵魂永生", "count": 6}, {"name": "梦、进化与价值完成", "count": 5}, {"name": "早期课第5册", "count": 3}, {"name": "未知的实相卷一", "count": 1}, {"name": "心灵的本质", "count": 1}, {"name": "时空之外", "count": 1}, {"name": "神奇之道", "count": 1}], "span": [1963, 1984], "stats": {"blocks": 9, "quotes": 120, "reading": 15, "reading_tagged": 0, "tagged": 0, "only_en": 14}};
